Subject: I2 verify scans live values once per boundary

What this does
  I2 verify scans live values once per boundary.

Why we need it
  The I2 promoted-slot check walked every live value once per promoted slot, quadratic in the frame size.

What it adds
  One pass over the live values per block boundary into `seen`, then a check of each slot's expected value.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
